            <ArticleTitle>[Inhibition, by electro-acupuncture, of the scalp evoked potential induced by painful stimulation of the tooth in man].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>584-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Scalp potentials evoked by electrical stimulation of the tooth pulp can be diminished in amplitude by electroacupuncture. This diminution goes generally in inverse with the increase in subjective pain threshold.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
